---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import ToolPage from "@bt/ui/ToolPage.astro";
import AdSlot from "@bt/ui/AdSlot.astro";
import HijriAgeCalc from "../../components/HijriAgeCalc.tsx";
---
<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Hijri age calculator: your age in Hijri and Gregorian years | Baitaan"
  description="Work out your age in the Hijri and Gregorian calendars in years, months and days, find your Hijri date of birth and your next Hijri birthday. Free, no sign-up."
>
  <ToolPage
    heading="Hijri age calculator"
    lead="Enter your date of birth in the Gregorian or Hijri calendar to see your age in both calendars, your matching date of birth and how many days you have lived."
    updated="Updated: November 2026"
  >
    <HijriAgeCalc client:load lang="en" />

    <Fragment slot="guide">
      <h2>Why is my Hijri age higher?</h2>
      <p>A Hijri year is about 11 days shorter than a Gregorian year, so your Hijri age gains roughly one year for every 33 Gregorian years. Someone who is 33 in Gregorian years is about 34 in Hijri years.</p>

      <h2>When is a Hijri age needed?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>In some government transactions and official forms in Saudi Arabia.</li>
        <li>To work out religious age limits and periods.</li>
        <li>To read the Hijri date of birth recorded in older documents.</li>
      </ul>

      <AdSlot slot="0000000000" label="Advertisement" />

      <p>The tool uses the Umm al-Qura calendar. If your country relied on moon sighting when you were born, your recorded Hijri date may differ by one day.</p>
      <p>To count the time between any two dates, use the <a class="text-teal-800 underline" href="/en/alfarq-bayna-tarikhayn/">days between two dates</a> calculator.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </ToolPage>
</Layout>
